  "prefLabel": "Fam 804.02 Contents of Screening Tool",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fam 804.02 Contents of Screening Tool. The purpose of using a screening tool is to gain information that will help in achieving the goal set out in Fam 801.01. In developing, adapting or using a published screening tool, a certified family mediator shall ensure that the screening tool includes, at a minimum:\n\n(a) Questions designed to explore whether domestic violence has occurred between the parties or is occurring;\n\n(b) Questions about specific behaviors in the following areas, including whether the behavior was recent, escalating, or both:\n\n(1) Control;\n\n(2) Coercion;\n\n(3) Intimidation; and\n\n(4) Violence;\n\n(c) Questions about the party’s fear of the other and sense of danger from the other.\n\nSource. #12687, eff 12-5-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/fam100-800.html"
}
